{"facts":[{"id":"fact_18","kind":"unknown","text":"Why is Warwick the smith growing more paranoid, adding lucky charms to his shop every day? Gill guessed it is to keep Ingrid away, and Ingrid says she climbs to his window every night to leave gifts and watch him sleep, which may be what he senses.","state":"open","change":"updated","ended_how":null,"learned_this_session":true,"definite_end":null,"possibly_moot":null,"certainty":"established","uncertain_reason":null,"about_thread":null,"also_bears_on":["thread_11"],"importance":"low","actionability":"medium","evidence":["prior","beat_13","beat_32"],"classification":{"serves_thread":"","significance":null,"commitment_type":null,"stake_basis":"","stake":null,"burden":null,"consequence":null,"blocks_thread":"","in_effect":null,"form":null,"helps_thread":"","role":null,"support_basis":"","goal_support":null,"action_basis":"","action_offered":null,"acquired_by_acting_on_opening":false,"grounding_justification":"The charm-covered shop is a conspicuous anomaly, and Ingrid's secret nightly visits give a likely but unconfirmed explanation.","grounding":"medium","investigative_depth_justification":"The answer would reveal whether Warwick senses Ingrid or fears something else, a hidden circumstance.","investigative_depth":"medium","narrative_payoff_justification":"Mildly amusing confirmation of the Ingrid romance; largely partly explained already.","narrative_payoff":"low","investigative_potential_justification":"Could be checked by speaking to Warwick or watching his house; little beyond that.","investigative_potential":"low","question_type":"open_ended","harm_origin":null,"negative_outcome_clarity_justification":"","negative_outcome_clarity":null,"outcome_severity_justification":"","outcome_severity":null,"evidentiary_strength_justification":"","evidentiary_strength":null,"evidence_of_progression_justification":"","evidence_of_progression":null,"preventability_justification":"","preventability":null}},{"id":"fact_new_1","kin